PATCH 239: faithful reconstruction of the MGAVIDEO pixel-mask span HIT-TEST FUN_0000_25d1
(asm-verified vs re_out/fist_mga_image.bin 0x25d1-0x2603).

Dispatched as the MGA far method vector DGROUP:0x6ac from the ENGINE cursor hit-test path
1eb4 -> 4aaa (patch 240 threads 4aaa's dropped cx/dx/bx args + captures this function's CF).
Under FIST_COOP_TICK=1 in-mission it SIGSEGVs because Ghidra dropped BOTH:
  (a) the DGROUP rebase of the 0x7c8 scanline-offset-table read `add dx,[si+0x7c8]` -- rendered as
      a bare near-NULL `*(int*)(param_1*2+0x7c8)` (deref of ~0x8bc -> SIGSEGV); patch-119/121 class;
  (b) the `push ds; mov ds,[bx]` span-data SEGMENT load -- rendered the span walk from a host
      `(uint*)0x0` (NULL deref) and at 4-byte `uint*` stride instead of the asm 2-byte `lods ax`.
Rebuilt in the DGROUP-offset model: rowtable at DGROUP:0x7c8 (word entries); span segment =
word[DGROUP:bx]; span WORDs walked from that segment offset 0.  Returns x86 CF via g_fist_cf
(stc=found/1, clc=not-found/0) which 4aaa consumes (`jb 0x4ae3` -> DGROUP:0x7aea).

asm map:
   si=cx; si+=si; dx += word[DG + cx*2 + 0x7c8]         ; target position
   di=0; ds = word[DG + bx]; S = ds<<4; si=0; ax=0
 L_add:  di += ax
 L_load: ax = word[S+si]; si += 2
         b0 = ax&1; ax >>= 1
         if (b0==0) { if(ax==0) ret clc; if(dx<di) ret clc; di+=ax; if(dx>=di) goto L_load; ret stc; }
         b1 = ax&1; ax >>= 1
         if (b1==0) { di += ax; goto L_load; }           ; jae 0x25e2 (add di,ax) then reload
         ax = word[S+si]; si += 2; di += ax; goto L_load  ; 0x25ed

Cascade-only: reached only via the in-mission 0x200-flag cursor track (the menu/dialog clicks take
4aaa's 0x180 branch, never [0x6ac]); the walk is bounded (uint16 si, seg<<4 <= 0xffff0) so it is
crash-free for any input -> gives FIST_COOP_TICK=1 a deterministic no-crash anchor.  BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL
for the 19 verify flows.  Source pristine; fist_mga.c via build/.  Portable C.
